DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The SecureTTY service module for PAM, ppaamm__sseeccuurreettttyy provides functional‐
     ity for only one PAM category: account management.  In terms of the
     _m_o_d_u_l_e_-_t_y_p_e parameter, this is the “account” feature.  It also provides
     null functions for authentication and session management.

   SSeeccuurreeTTTTYY AAccccoouunntt MMaannaaggeemmeenntt MMoodduullee
     The SecureTTY account management component (ppaamm__ssmm__aacccctt__mmggmmtt()), returns
     failure if the user is attempting to authenticate as superuser, and the
     process is attached to an insecure TTY.  In all other cases, the module
     returns success.

     A TTY is considered secure if it is listed in _/_e_t_c_/_t_t_y_s and has the
     TTY_SECURE flag set.

     The following options may be passed to the authentication module:

     ddeebbuugg    syslog(3) debugging information at LOG_DEBUG level.

     nnoo__wwaarrnn  suppress warning messages to the user.  These messages include
              reasons why the user's authentication attempt was declined.

